# Settings for the demo stack. Copy to demo/.env and uncomment one block.
# `.env` is git-ignored; a member key must never be committed.

## No model (default)
# The stack starts with no model backend. The Ask box answers
# "no model backend configured" (503); everything else in the demo works.
# FREEHOLD_LLM_BACKEND=none

## Model at a federated operator
# The agent sends the holder's ask to a model run by an operator. The custody
# rung must say where the model really runs, because every rule's custody
# ceiling is checked against it: `community_node` for a node run by someone
# the holder knows, `federated_operator` for an operator accountable through
# community governance. Only the one entry a rule names, and the question,
# leave the holder's machine; the audit line is written before the call.
# FREEHOLD_LLM_BACKEND=http
# The operator's gateway, an OpenAI-compatible endpoint over https (public CA).
# FREEHOLD_LLM_URL=https://<gateway>/v1
# A member key from the operator, sent as a Bearer token. Never commit it.
# FREEHOLD_LLM_API_KEY=replace-with-the-member-key
# The model name the operator exposes (our built-in tier names are not theirs).
# FREEHOLD_LLM_MODEL=replace-with-the-operator-model
# FREEHOLD_LLM_CUSTODY=federated_operator
